ID: US-007
Title: Sequencing, truncation, snapshot, and session_warning

Story details:
### US-007: Sequencing, truncation, snapshot, and session_warning
Status: in_progress
Depends on: US-006

Description:
As a client, I need deterministic sequencing and truncation recovery so output remains consistent under high volume.

Acceptance Criteria:
- [ ] Output seq is strictly monotonic per session; next_seq equals last delivered + 1
- [ ] When buffer is truncated, responses/events set `truncated: true` and include `snapshot`
- [ ] Emit `session_warning` with reason `buffer_truncated` when truncation occurs
- [ ] Example: writing > 512 KB to a session yields `truncated: true` with a snapshot on next poll
- [ ] Negative: if snapshot alone exceeds max payload, emit `payload_too_large` warning and close connection


If the story details are empty or missing, STOP and report that the PRD story format could not be parsed.

